-is a clean-room analytic field (plane front + value-noise bend + rounded-rect
-SDF + 2D gaussian core); it shares only the unprotectable high-level idea of a
-“scalar heat → thermal color ramp” with Paper Shaders.
-
-Earlier MR9 research prototypes (the “Heatmap Literal Fidelity” spike and its
-core-removal / latent-carrier successors) **did** closely adapt
-`heatmap.ts` from `@paper-design/shaders@0.0.80` (Apache-2.0). Those prototypes
-were rejected during visual review and their Paper-derived shader helpers,
-boundary-texture preprocessing (`blurGray` / `multiPassBlurGray`,
-`rasterizeHeatmap*`), and renderer-owned texture lifecycle were **removed**
-when the analytic baseline was restored. They are retained only as historical
-research evidence under `.trellis/tasks/08-15-mr9-fullscreen-activation-fx-
-progress-visual-refinement/research/` and are not part of any shipped or
-active source path.
-
-The Apache-2.0 text and Paper NOTICE are reproduced below for attribution
-and historical traceability of that research.
+## License status: one active Paper-derived Lab-only preprocessing spike
+
+The **Lab-only Paper processed-silhouette spike** in
+`src/presentation/main-window/ExpandedPresentationSurface.tsx` is an **active
+Apache-2.0 derivative** of the geometry-agnostic preprocessing and scalar
+causality of `heatmap.ts` from `@paper-design/shaders@0.0.80` (Copyright 2026
+Paper, https://shaders.paper.design). It is gated behind a Lab-only `paper`
+prop that production never sets; it contributes exactly one CPU-built
+processed RGBA texture (`blurGray` / `multiPassBlurGray` integral-image box
+blur + a rounded-rect mask rasterizer) and one inner/outer/contour scalar
+composition, sampled by the existing single shader. Paper's
+logo/diamond/image-frame geometry, ShaderMount/ShaderSizing React runtime,
+and per-pixel helpers are NOT used; the exact Ameow 200x200/r16 panel
+silhouette is the sole source.
+
+### Modified Derivative Notice
+
+Per Apache-2.0 §4(b), this repository carries prominent modification notices:
+
+- The source file `src/presentation/main-window/ExpandedPresentationSurface.tsx`
+  starts with a `MODIFIED DERIVATIVE — Paper Heatmap mechanics (Apache-2.0)`
+  header naming the upstream (`@paper-design/shaders@0.0.80`, `heatmap.ts`,
+  Copyright 2026 Paper, https://shaders.paper.design) and describing what was
+  adapted and what was excluded.
+- adapted source: `src/presentation/main-window/ExpandedPresentationSurface.tsx`
+  (Lab-only `paper` mode: CPU preprocessing + shader `paperOutput`).
+- This file reproduces the upstream NOTICE and the full Apache-2.0 text below.
+- Ameow's root `LICENSE` (MIT) is unchanged and governs all non-adapted code.
 
